# T3b — a uid missing from the allowlist must be refused.
# The two gates are measured separately, because reporting the filesystem
# gate as if it were the allowlist is how this experiment first misled
# itself (see REPORT §6, deviation 2).
#   gate 1 (kernel): socket mode 0600 + parent directory mode
#   gate 2 (helper): SO_PEERCRED uid vs --allow-uid

## case 1: defaults (parent 0700, socket 0600)
  socket mode=600 uid=0
  uid5 connect -> REFUSED_BY_KERNEL errno=13 Permission denied

## case 2: parent 0777 and socket 0666, so gate 1 is wide open.
#          Any refusal now must come from SO_PEERCRED.
  socket mode=666 uid=0
  uid5 connect -> REFUSED errno=13 Permission denied
  allowed uid0 -> {"ok":true,"opcode":"Describe","data":{"no_new_privs":true,"ops":["Describe","StatPath","ReadSmall","ListDir"],"root":"/tmp/li-phase0-0g-f8uh0T/t3b/root","uid":0}}

## audit records for the refused connection (case 2)
  (none)
